{#-
  ============================================================================
  UC13 — FINAL DILIGENCE REPORT  ·  final_report.html.j2
  ============================================================================
  PROPOSAL / v0.1 — structure and format are open for review.

  WHAT THIS TEMPLATE IS
    The full report deliverable, rebuilt as a 10-page visual document a PE VP
    can read in 10 minutes and then use as the reference for the deal. It
    replaces the current text-only `full_report.md.j2`. It sits alongside,
    and does not replace, `rainmaker_opportunity_summary.html.j2` (the 3-page
    executive review) — the MPS page is intentionally rendered in BOTH, so
    the two documents agree.

  HARD RULES FOR WHOEVER GENERATES AGAINST THIS TEMPLATE
    R1 · The template is dumb. Every number, every percentage, every bar
         height arrives pre-computed from `report` (see final_report_view.py).
         No arithmetic, no parsing, no LLM calls in here.
    R2 · Nothing is fabricated. A missing figure renders as an explicit
         "Not extracted" / "—" state, never as an estimate, and never as a
         chart with an invented bar.
    R3 · Caps are part of the format, not a suggestion. Every list below is
         sliced. If an agent produces 30 risks, this report shows the top 8
         and the appendix says how many were suppressed. Length discipline is
         what makes the report readable.
    R4 · One page = one question a VP actually asks. If a section does not
         answer one of the ten questions on the contents page, it belongs in
         an appendix or in the workstream detail files, not here.
    R5 · Every claim carries a source. Citations are footnote markers
         (`cite` fields), never inline bracketed doc names in the prose.

  RENDER
    ReportRenderer().render(bundle, "final_report.html.j2", report=<view>,
                            mps=<mps projection>, brand_logo_data_uri=...)
    Primary engine WeasyPrint (full SVG + flex fidelity). The PyMuPDF Story
    fallback degrades charts; ship the HTML when that path is taken.
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ report.meta.company_name | default('Company', true) }} — Final Diligence Report</title>
<style>
  /* --- Page + palette: inherited from rainmaker_opportunity_summary.html.j2
         so the two deliverables look like one family. -------------------- */
  @page { size: A4 portrait; margin: 14mm 14mm 12mm 14mm; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1A1A1A; font-size: 9pt; line-height: 1.35; margin: 0;
  }
  .page { page-break-after: always; }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }

  /* Screen preview only. In print, @page owns the margins and this block does
     not apply. On screen there is no @page, so the body needs its own gutter or
     the text sits flush against the viewport edge — which is what a reviewer
     opening the HTML in a browser or an embedded viewer sees.

     This block MUST come after the base `body` rule: both are single-element
     selectors, so at equal specificity the later one wins, and the base rule's
     `margin: 0` silently cancels the auto centring if this sits above it.

     max-width 202mm + 10mm side padding reproduces the printed content width
     (A4 210mm less 14mm margins = 182mm) exactly, so line breaks and chart
     proportions on screen match the PDF. */
  @media screen {
    body {
      max-width: 202mm;
      margin: 0 auto;
      margin-inline: auto;
      padding: 8mm 10mm;
    }
    .page { border-bottom: 0.5pt dashed #BFD0E8; padding-bottom: 8mm; margin-bottom: 10mm; }
    .page:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  }


  h1 { color: #1F3864; font-size: 20pt; margin: 0 0 1mm 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2.section { color: #1F3864; font-size: 14pt; margin: 0 0 0.5mm 0; }
  h3.block {
    color: #FFF; background: #1F3864; font-size: 7.5pt; font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 1.2mm 2.5mm; margin: 0 0 2mm 0;
  }
  h3.block.warn { background: #C2600D; }
  h3.block.plain { background: #F2F4F7; color: #1F3864; }
  h4.mini { color: #595959; font-size: 7.5pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin: 0 0 1.5mm 0; }
  .eyebrow { color: #C2600D; font-weight: bold; font-size: 8pt; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .subtitle { color: #595959; font-size: 9.5pt; }
  .meta { color: #595959; font-size: 7.5pt; }
  .divider { border-top: 2pt solid #1F3864; margin: 2.5mm 0 4mm 0; }

  .running-header {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline;
    color: #595959; font-size: 7pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    border-bottom: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; padding-bottom: 1.2mm; margin-bottom: 3.5mm;
  }
  .running-header .company { color: #1F3864; font-weight: bold; }
  .footer { color: #595959; font-size: 6.5pt; border-top: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; padding-top: 1.2mm; margin-top: 4mm; }

  /* --- Callouts ------------------------------------------------------- */
  .verdict { border-left: 3pt solid #1F3864; background: #EEF3FA; padding: 3mm 4mm; margin: 0 0 4mm 0; }
  .verdict .label { color: #1F3864; font-size: 8pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .verdict .call { font-size: 13pt; font-weight: bold; color: #1F3864; display: block; margin: 0.5mm 0 1mm 0; }
  .verdict.pass { border-left-color: #C2600D; background: #FCEEE0; }
  .verdict.pass .call, .verdict.pass .label { color: #C2600D; }
  .one-liner { font-style: italic; background: #F2F4F7; border-left: 3pt solid #BFD0E8; padding: 2mm 3.5mm; margin: 0 0 4mm 0; }
  .take { background: #F2F4F7; padding: 2mm 3mm; margin: 2mm 0 0 0; font-size: 8.5pt; }
  .take strong { color: #1F3864; }
  .nodata { color: #595959; font-style: italic; font-size: 8.5pt; }

  /* --- Tiles ---------------------------------------------------------- */
  .tiles { display: flex; gap: 2.5mm; margin: 0 0 4mm 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .tile { flex: 1 1 28mm; background: #F2F4F7; border: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; border-radius: 1.5mm; padding: 2.5mm 2mm; text-align: center; }
  .tile .value { display: block; color: #1F3864; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.1; }
  .tile .label { display: block; color: #595959; font-size: 6.5pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; margin-top: 0.8mm; }
  .tile .sub { display: block; color: #1A1A1A; font-size: 7pt; margin-top: 0.5mm; }
  .tile.flag { border-color: #C2600D; background: #FCEEE0; }
  .tile.flag .value { color: #C2600D; }

  /* --- Tables --------------------------------------------------------- */
  table.dt { width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0 0 3mm 0; }
  table.dt th, table.dt td { border-bottom: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; padding: 1.2mm 1.8mm; text-align: right; vertical-align: top; font-size: 8pt; }
  table.dt th { color: #FFF; background: #1F3864; font-size: 6.8pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; font-weight: bold; }
  table.dt th:first-child, table.dt td:first-child { text-align: left; }
  table.dt tr.total td { background: #EEF3FA; font-weight: bold; color: #1F3864; }
  table.dt tr.sub td:first-child { padding-left: 4mm; color: #595959; }
  table.dt td.calc { background: #EEF3FA; font-weight: bold; color: #1F3864; }
  table.dt th.calc { background: #17284C; }
  table.dt.left td, table.dt.left th { text-align: left; }
  .chip { display: inline-block; padding: 0.3mm 1.6mm; border-radius: 1mm; font-size: 6.8pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
  .chip.high { background: #F8D7D5; color: #9C2A20; }
  .chip.medium { background: #FCEEE0; color: #C2600D; }
  .chip.low { background: #E4EFE1; color: #3D6B34; }
  .chip.neutral { background: #F2F4F7; color: #595959; }
  sup.cite { color: #4A72B8; font-size: 6pt; }

  /* --- Layout helpers ------------------------------------------------- */
  .cols-2 { display: flex; gap: 5mm; margin-bottom: 4mm; }
  .cols-2 > * { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .cols-3 { display: flex; gap: 4mm; margin-bottom: 4mm; }
  .cols-3 > * { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .card { border: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; border-radius: 1.5mm; overflow: hidden; }
  .card .body { padding: 0 2.5mm 2mm 2.5mm; }
  ul.b { margin: 0 0 2mm 0; padding-left: 3.5mm; }
  ul.b li { margin-bottom: 0.8mm; }
  ol.q { margin: 0; padding-left: 5mm; }
  ol.q li { margin-bottom: 1.5mm; }
  ol.q .cat { color: #C2600D; font-size: 6.8pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  ol.q .why { color: #595959; font-size: 7.5pt; display: block; }
  .legend { display: flex; gap: 4mm; flex-wrap: wrap; color: #595959; font-size: 7pt; margin: 0 0 2mm 0; }
  .legend .k { display: inline-block; width: 2.4mm; height: 2.4mm; border-radius: 0.4mm; margin-right: 1mm; vertical-align: -0.2mm; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  /* --- MPS table: lifted verbatim from rainmaker_opportunity_summary.html.j2.
         Keep in sync with that file, or better, share one partial. ------- */
  .mps-page { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  table.mps-table { width: 100%; table-layout: fixed; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.5mm 0; }
  table.mps-table th, table.mps-table td {
    border-bottom: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; padding: 0.8mm 2mm; text-align: left; vertical-align: top;
    font-size: 7.3pt; line-height: 1.1; overflow: hidden;
  }
  table.mps-table th { color: #fff; background: #1F3864; font-size: 7pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  table.mps-table th.mps-category-col, table.mps-table td.mps-category-col { background: #1F3864; color: #fff; font-weight: bold; }
  table.mps-table tr { page-break-inside: avoid; }
  table.mps-table td.mps-score-col { text-align: center; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; color: #1F3864; }
  table.mps-table td.mps-commentary-col ul.bullets { margin: 0; padding-left: 3mm; }
  table.mps-table td.mps-commentary-col li { margin-bottom: 0.3mm; }
  table.mps-table li.mps-counter-evidence { color: #595959; font-style: italic; }
  table.mps-table tr.mps-total-row td { border-bottom: none; border-top: 1pt solid #1F3864; }
  .mps-legend { color: #595959; font-size: 7pt; margin: 0 0 1mm 0; }
  .mps-footer-note { color: #1F3864; font-weight: bold; font-size: 9pt; margin-top: 1mm; }

  /* Contents page */
  table.toc { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  table.toc td { padding: 1.8mm 2mm; border-bottom: 0.5pt solid #BFD0E8; font-size: 9pt; vertical-align: top; }
  table.toc td.n { width: 8mm; color: #C2600D; font-weight: bold; }
  table.toc td.p { width: 10mm; text-align: right; color: #595959; }
  table.toc .q { color: #595959; font-size: 8pt; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

{#- =====================================================================
    MACROS — the visual vocabulary of the report.
    Every macro takes ALREADY-NORMALISED input: `pct` fields are 0–100 and
    computed by the view layer. A macro never scales, never parses, never
    guesses. `None` inputs are drawn as gaps, not as zero.
    ===================================================================== -#}

{%- macro running_header(report, section, page_no) -%}
<div class="running-header">
  <span><span class="company">{{ report.meta.company_name }}</span> · Final Diligence Report</span>
  <span>{{ section }} · {{ page_no }}</span>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro page_footer(report) -%}
<div class="footer">
  {{ report.meta.status }} · Generated {{ report.meta.date }} · Mode: {{ report.meta.mode_label }} · Overall confidence: {{ report.meta.overall_confidence }}
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro nodata(what) -%}
<p class="nodata">{{ what }} — not extracted from the data room. See the gap list on the appendix page.</p>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- CHART 1 · Grouped column chart with an overlaid margin line.
    Use for: revenue + EBITDA vs prior years, forecast vs historical.
    Input: {series:[{label, bar1_pct, bar1_value, bar2_pct, bar2_value,
                     line_pct, line_value}], bar1_name, bar2_name, line_name,
            axis_max_label, footnote}
    `*_pct` is height as % of the chart's own max. `None` = bar omitted. -#}
{%- macro chart_columns(c) -%}
{%- set n = c.series | length -%}
{%- if n == 0 -%}{{ nodata(c.bar1_name) }}{%- else -%}
{%- set step = (300 / n) | round(2) -%}
<svg viewBox="0 0 340 132" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
  {%- for g in [0, 25, 50, 75, 100] %}
  <line x1="30" y1="{{ 104 - (g * 0.92) }}" x2="336" y2="{{ 104 - (g * 0.92) }}"
        stroke="{{ '#BFD0E8' if g > 0 else '#595959' }}" stroke-width="{{ 0.7 if g == 0 else 0.4 }}"/>
  {%- endfor %}
  <text x="28" y="14" font-size="6" fill="#595959" text-anchor="end">{{ c.axis_max_label | default('', true) }}</text>
  <text x="28" y="106" font-size="6" fill="#595959" text-anchor="end">0</text>
  {%- for s in c.series %}
  {%- set cx = 30 + (step * loop.index0) + (step / 2) -%}
    {%- if s.bar1_pct is not none %}
    <rect x="{{ (cx - 13) | round(2) }}" y="{{ (104 - (s.bar1_pct * 0.92)) | round(2) }}"
          width="12" height="{{ (s.bar1_pct * 0.92) | round(2) }}" fill="#1F3864"/>
    <text x="{{ (cx - 7) | round(2) }}" y="{{ (100 - (s.bar1_pct * 0.92)) | round(2) }}"
          font-size="6.2" fill="#1F3864" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">{{ s.bar1_value }}</text>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if s.bar2_pct is not none %}
    <rect x="{{ (cx + 1) | round(2) }}" y="{{ (104 - (s.bar2_pct * 0.92)) | round(2) }}"
          width="12" height="{{ (s.bar2_pct * 0.92) | round(2) }}" fill="#9FB8DC"/>
    <text x="{{ (cx + 7) | round(2) }}" y="{{ (100 - (s.bar2_pct * 0.92)) | round(2) }}"
          font-size="6.2" fill="#4A72B8" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">{{ s.bar2_value }}</text>
    {%- endif %}
  <text x="{{ cx | round(2) }}" y="115" font-size="6.4" fill="#1A1A1A" text-anchor="middle">{{ s.label }}</text>
  {%- endfor %}
  {#- Margin line: only drawn across periods that actually have a value. -#}
  {%- set pts = [] -%}
  {%- for s in c.series -%}
    {%- if s.line_pct is not none -%}
      {%- set _ = pts.append(((30 + (step * loop.index0) + (step / 2)) | round(2) ~ ',' ~ ((104 - (s.line_pct * 0.92)) | round(2)))) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if pts | length > 1 %}
  <polyline points="{{ pts | join(' ') }}" fill="none" stroke="#C2600D" stroke-width="1.2"/>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- for s in c.series %}
    {%- if s.line_pct is not none %}
    {%- set cx = 30 + (step * loop.index0) + (step / 2) -%}
    <circle cx="{{ cx | round(2) }}" cy="{{ (104 - (s.line_pct * 0.92)) | round(2) }}" r="2" fill="#C2600D"/>
    <text x="{{ (cx + 4) | round(2) }}" y="{{ (99 - (s.line_pct * 0.92)) | round(2) }}"
          font-size="6.2" fill="#C2600D" text-anchor="start" font-weight="bold">{{ s.line_value }}</text>
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
  <text x="30" y="128" font-size="5.8" fill="#595959">{{ c.footnote | default('', true) }}</text>
</svg>
<div class="legend">
  <span><span class="k" style="background:#1F3864"></span>{{ c.bar1_name }}</span>
  {%- if c.bar2_name %}<span><span class="k" style="background:#9FB8DC"></span>{{ c.bar2_name }}</span>{% endif %}
  {%- if c.line_name %}<span><span class="k" style="background:#C2600D"></span>{{ c.line_name }}</span>{% endif %}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- CHART 2 · Horizontal bars with an optional threshold marker.
    Use for: customer / referral-source concentration (threshold = the
    Rallyday screen: 25% tech services, 20% healthcare services), payor
    concentration, vendor dependence.
    Input: {bars:[{label, value, pct, flag}], threshold_pct, threshold_label} -#}
{%- macro chart_hbars(c) -%}
{%- if (c.bars | length) == 0 -%}{{ nodata(c.title | default('Concentration', true)) }}{%- else -%}
{%- set row_h = 12 -%}
{%- set x0 = 92 -%}{%- set w = 1.4 -%}
<svg viewBox="0 0 260 {{ (c.bars | length) * row_h + 14 }}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
  {%- if c.threshold_pct is not none %}
  <line x1="{{ (x0 + (c.threshold_pct * w)) | round(2) }}" y1="2"
        x2="{{ (x0 + (c.threshold_pct * w)) | round(2) }}" y2="{{ (c.bars | length) * row_h + 1 }}"
        stroke="#C2600D" stroke-width="0.7" stroke-dasharray="2,1.5"/>
  <text x="{{ (x0 + (c.threshold_pct * w) - 1) | round(2) }}" y="{{ (c.bars | length) * row_h + 9 }}"
        font-size="5.6" fill="#C2600D" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">{{ c.threshold_label }}</text>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- for b in c.bars %}
  {%- set y = (loop.index0 * row_h) + 2 -%}
  <text x="0" y="{{ y + 6.5 }}" font-size="7" fill="#1A1A1A">{{ b.label }}</text>
  <rect x="{{ x0 }}" y="{{ y }}" width="{{ (b.pct * w) | round(2) }}" height="8"
        fill="{{ '#C2600D' if b.flag else '#1F3864' }}" rx="0.6"/>
  <text x="{{ (x0 + 3 + (b.pct * w)) | round(2) }}" y="{{ y + 6.5 }}" font-size="7"
        fill="{{ '#C2600D' if b.flag else '#1F3864' }}" font-weight="bold">{{ b.value }}</text>
  {%- endfor %}
</svg>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- CHART 3 · 100% stacked bar with legend.
    Use for: revenue mix (recurring vs project), payor mix, client
    distribution by segment / geography / service line.
    Input: {segments:[{label, pct, value}], caption} — pct must sum to ~100. -#}
{%- macro chart_stack(c) -%}
{%- if (c.segments | length) == 0 -%}{{ nodata(c.caption | default('Mix', true)) }}{%- else -%}
{%- set palette = ['#1F3864', '#4A72B8', '#9FB8DC', '#C2600D', '#E8A33D', '#A6A6A6'] -%}
<svg viewBox="0 0 340 26" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
  {%- set ns = namespace(x=0) -%}
  {%- for s in c.segments %}
  {%- set w = (s.pct * 3.4) | round(2) -%}
  <rect x="{{ ns.x }}" y="2" width="{{ w }}" height="14" fill="{{ palette[loop.index0 % 6] }}"/>
  {%- if s.pct >= 9 %}
  <text x="{{ (ns.x + (w / 2)) | round(2) }}" y="11.5" font-size="6.4" fill="#FFF" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="bold">{{ s.value }}</text>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- set ns.x = ns.x + w -%}
  {%- endfor %}
</svg>
<div class="legend">
  {%- for s in c.segments %}
  <span><span class="k" style="background:{{ palette[loop.index0 % 6] }}"></span>{{ s.label }} {{ s.value }}</span>
  {%- endfor %}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- CHART 4 · Bullet bars — actual value against a Rallyday screen threshold.
    Use for: the KPI scorecard. This is the chart that makes the sector
    guidelines visible instead of buried in prose.
    Input: {rows:[{name, value, pct, threshold_pct, threshold_label, flag}]} -#}
{%- macro chart_bullets(c) -%}
{%- if (c.rows | length) == 0 -%}{{ nodata('Operating KPIs') }}{%- else -%}
{%- set row_h = 13 -%}
<svg viewBox="0 0 340 {{ (c.rows | length) * row_h + 4 }}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img">
  {%- for r in c.rows %}
  {%- set y = (loop.index0 * row_h) + 2 -%}
  <text x="0" y="{{ y + 5 }}" font-size="6.6" fill="#1A1A1A">{{ r.name }}</text>
  <rect x="118" y="{{ y }}" width="150" height="8" fill="#F2F4F7"/>
  {%- if r.pct is not none %}
  <rect x="118" y="{{ y }}" width="{{ (r.pct * 1.5) | round(2) }}" height="8"
        fill="{{ '#C2600D' if r.flag else '#1F3864' }}"/>
  {%- else %}
  <text x="122" y="{{ y + 6 }}" font-size="6" fill="#595959" font-style="italic">not extracted</text>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if r.threshold_pct is not none %}
  <line x1="{{ (118 + (r.threshold_pct * 1.5)) | round(2) }}" y1="{{ y - 1.5 }}"
        x2="{{ (118 + (r.threshold_pct * 1.5)) | round(2) }}" y2="{{ y + 9.5 }}"
        stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="1"/>
  {%- endif %}
  <text x="272" y="{{ y + 6 }}" font-size="6.4" fill="{{ '#C2600D' if r.flag else '#1F3864' }}" font-weight="bold">{{ r.value | default('—', true) }}</text>
  <text x="304" y="{{ y + 6 }}" font-size="5.8" fill="#595959">{{ r.threshold_label | default('', true) }}</text>
  {%- endfor %}
</svg>
<div class="legend">
  <span><span class="k" style="background:#1F3864"></span>At or above screen</span>
  <span><span class="k" style="background:#C2600D"></span>Below screen — flagged</span>
  <span><span class="k" style="background:#1A1A1A;width:0.8mm"></span>Rallyday threshold</span>
</div>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Severity chip, driven by the view layer's own severity mapping. -#}
{%- macro sev(label, cls) -%}<span class="chip {{ cls | default('neutral', true) }}">{{ label }}</span>{%- endmacro -%}


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 1 · COVER + THE CALL
    Question answered: "Do we pursue this, and what is the one-line reason?"
    The recommendation goes first. A VP should not have to read to page 6.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-start;">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Final Diligence Report</div>
      <h1>{{ report.meta.company_name }}</h1>
      <div class="subtitle">{{ report.meta.sector_label | default('', true) }}</div>
    </div>
    {%- if brand_logo_data_uri %}
    <img src="{{ brand_logo_data_uri }}" alt="" style="max-height:10mm">
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="meta" style="margin-bottom:4mm;">
    Prepared for {{ report.meta.prepared_for }} · {{ report.meta.date }} ·
    Generated from {{ report.meta.mode_label }} ·
    {{ report.meta.doc_count | default('—', true) }} documents indexed ·
    Overall confidence: <strong>{{ report.meta.overall_confidence }}</strong>
  </div>

  {%- set rec = report.headline.recommendation %}
  <div class="verdict {{ 'pass' if rec.tone == 'pass' else '' }}">
    <span class="label">Recommendation</span>
    <span class="call">{{ rec.verdict | default('Not yet concluded', true) }}</span>
    {%- if rec.rationale %}<div>{{ rec.rationale }}</div>{% endif %}
    {%- if rec.conditions %}
    <div style="margin-top:1.5mm;"><strong>Conditional on:</strong>
      <ul class="b" style="margin-top:0.8mm;">
        {%- for cond in rec.conditions[:3] %}<li>{{ cond }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="one-liner">{{ report.headline.one_liner | default('One-line business description not yet synthesised.', true) }}</div>

  <h3 class="block">The Numbers That Drive The Call</h3>
  <div class="tiles">
    {%- for t in report.headline.tiles[:6] %}
    <div class="tile {{ 'flag' if t.flag else '' }}">
      <span class="value">{{ t.value | default('—', true) }}</span>
      <span class="label">{{ t.label }}</span>
      {%- if t.sub %}<span class="sub">{{ t.sub }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- else %}
    <div class="tile"><span class="value">—</span><span class="label">Headline metrics not extracted</span></div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h3 class="block">Why This Could Work — Top 3</h3>
      <ul class="b">
        {%- for item in report.headline.thesis[:3] %}<li>{{ item }}{% if item is string %}{% endif %}</li>
        {%- else %}<li class="nodata">Investment thesis not yet synthesised.</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 class="block warn">What Could Break It — Top 3</h3>
      <ul class="b">
        {%- for item in report.headline.watchouts[:3] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>
        {%- else %}<li class="nodata">Watchouts not yet synthesised.</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 2 · CONTENTS — one page per question.
    Kept because it is the fastest way for a VP to jump to the one section
    they care about, and because it forces R4 discipline on us.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Contents', 2) }}
  <h2 class="section">What this report answers</h2>
  <p class="meta" style="margin-bottom:4mm;">Ten pages, ten questions. Workstream detail, full reconciliation logs and source extracts live in the accompanying files, not here.</p>
  <table class="toc">
    {%- for item in report.contents %}
    <tr>
      <td class="n">{{ item.no }}</td>
      <td><strong>{{ item.title }}</strong><div class="q">{{ item.question }}</div></td>
      <td class="p">{{ item.page }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 3 · BUSINESS & REVENUE MODEL
    Question: "What is this business and how does it actually make money?"
    Visual: revenue mix stack + client / segment distribution.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Business & Revenue Model', 3) }}
  <h2 class="section">1 · Business and revenue model</h2>

  {%- if report.business.core_business %}
  <div class="one-liner">
    {%- for line in report.business.core_business %}<div>{{ line }}</div>{% endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3 class="block">What The Business Does</h3>
      <div class="body"><ul class="b">
        {%- for b in report.business.what_it_does[:4] %}<li>{{ b }}</li>
        {%- else %}<li class="nodata">Business overview not extracted.</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 class="block">How It Makes Money</h3>
      <div class="body"><ul class="b">
        {%- for b in report.business.how_it_makes_money[:4] %}<li>{{ b }}</li>
        {%- else %}<li class="nodata">Revenue model not extracted.</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Revenue mix — durability</h4>
      {{ chart_stack(report.business.revenue_mix) }}
      <p class="meta">{{ report.business.revenue_mix.caption | default('', true) }}</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Client distribution — {{ report.business.client_distribution.dimension | default('segment', true) }}</h4>
      {{ chart_stack(report.business.client_distribution) }}
      <p class="meta">{{ report.business.client_distribution.caption | default('', true) }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="block">Performance By {{ report.business.performance_by.dimension | default('Segment', true) }}</h3>
  {{ chart_columns(report.business.performance_by.chart) }}
  {%- if report.business.performance_by.rows %}
  <table class="dt">
    <tr>
      <th>{{ report.business.performance_by.dimension | default('Segment', true) }}</th>
      <th>Revenue</th><th>% of total</th><th>Gross margin</th><th>Growth YoY</th><th class="calc">Read</th>
    </tr>
    {%- for r in report.business.performance_by.rows[:6] %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ r.name }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.revenue | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.share | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.gross_margin | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.growth | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td class="calc">{{ sev(r.read_label, r.read_class) }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if report.business.take %}<div class="take"><strong>Analyst take.</strong> {{ report.business.take }}</div>{% endif %}
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 4 · FINANCIAL PERFORMANCE
    Question: "Is the financial story improving, and is it real?"
    Visual: the generic P&L block (works for any company — every row is
    optional and drops out if the agent did not extract it) + the
    revenue/EBITDA vs prior years chart.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Financial Performance', 4) }}
  <h2 class="section">2 · Financial performance</h2>

  <h3 class="block">P&amp;L Summary — {{ report.financials.table.unit_label | default('as reported', true) }}</h3>
  {%- if report.financials.table.periods %}
  <table class="dt">
    <tr>
      <th style="width:32%">{{ report.financials.table.currency | default('$', true) }} {{ report.financials.table.unit | default('', true) }}</th>
      {%- for p in report.financials.table.periods %}<th>{{ p }}</th>{% endfor %}
      <th class="calc">{{ report.financials.table.calc_col_label | default('CAGR', true) }}</th>
    </tr>
    {#- Row set is generic and self-pruning: revenue → COGS → gross profit →
        GM% → opex → EBITDA → EBITDA% → adjusted EBITDA → adj. margin →
        capex → FCF proxy. Rows the agent never extracted are dropped by the
        view layer, so a services business and a SaaS business both render
        cleanly from the same block. -#}
    {%- for row in report.financials.table.rows %}
    <tr class="{{ 'total' if row.emphasis == 'total' else ('sub' if row.emphasis == 'sub' else '') }}">
      <td>{{ row.label }}{% if row.cite %}<sup class="cite">{{ row.cite }}</sup>{% endif %}</td>
      {%- for cell in row.cells %}<td>{{ cell | default('—', true) }}</td>{% endfor %}
      <td class="calc">{{ row.calc | default('—', true) }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- else %}{{ nodata('P&L') }}{% endif %}

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Revenue vs prior years, with EBITDA margin</h4>
      {{ chart_columns(report.financials.trend_chart) }}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Reported vs adjusted EBITDA</h4>
      {{ chart_columns(report.financials.ebitda_chart) }}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">What the trend says</h4>
      <ul class="b">
        {%- for o in report.financials.observations[:4] %}<li>{{ o }}</li>
        {%- else %}<li class="nodata">No financial observations synthesised.</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      {%- if report.financials.bridge %}
      <h4 class="mini">Growth bridge — latest period</h4>
      <table class="dt left">
        {%- for b in report.financials.bridge[:5] %}
        <tr><td>{{ b.driver }}</td><td style="text-align:right">{{ b.value }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if report.financials.take %}<div class="take"><strong>Analyst take.</strong> {{ report.financials.take }}</div>{% endif %}
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 5 · CUSTOMER QUALITY & CONCENTRATION
    Question: "Is the revenue durable, and who could take it away?"
    Visual: concentration bars against the Rallyday threshold.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Customer Quality', 5) }}
  <h2 class="section">3 · Customer quality and concentration</h2>

  <div class="tiles">
    {%- for t in report.customers.tiles[:5] %}
    <div class="tile {{ 'flag' if t.flag else '' }}">
      <span class="value">{{ t.value | default('—', true) }}</span><span class="label">{{ t.label }}</span>
      {%- if t.sub %}<span class="sub">{{ t.sub }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Concentration — share of revenue</h4>
      {{ chart_hbars(report.customers.concentration) }}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Retention and tenure</h4>
      {%- if report.customers.retention_rows %}
      <table class="dt">
        <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th><th>Screen</th></tr>
        {%- for r in report.customers.retention_rows[:6] %}
        <tr><td>{{ r.metric }}</td><td>{{ r.value | default('—', true) }}</td><td>{{ sev(r.read_label, r.read_class) }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
      {%- else %}{{ nodata('Retention metrics') }}{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if report.customers.top_customers %}
  <h3 class="block">Top Accounts</h3>
  <table class="dt">
    <tr><th style="width:26%">Account</th><th>% of revenue</th><th>Trend</th><th>Gross margin</th><th>Contract status</th><th>Tenure</th></tr>
    {%- for c in report.customers.top_customers[:5] %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ c.name }}{% if c.cite %}<sup class="cite">{{ c.cite }}</sup>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ c.share | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.trend | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.gross_margin | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.contract_status | default('—', true) }}</td>
      <td>{{ c.tenure | default('—', true) }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if report.customers.take %}<div class="take"><strong>Analyst take.</strong> {{ report.customers.take }}</div>{% endif %}
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 6 · KPI SCORECARD vs RALLYDAY SCREENS
    Question: "Where does this business sit against how we screen its sector?"
    Visual: bullet bars. The sector overlay drives which KPIs appear.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'KPI Scorecard', 6) }}
  <h2 class="section">4 · Operating KPIs against our screens</h2>
  <p class="meta" style="margin-bottom:3mm;">
    Sector overlay applied: <strong>{{ report.kpis.overlay_label | default('not determined', true) }}</strong>.
    Thresholds are the directional first-pass screens, not hard rules — materiality is the deal team's call.
  </p>

  {{ chart_bullets(report.kpis) }}

  {%- if report.kpis.flagged %}
  <h3 class="block warn">Flagged — And What It Means</h3>
  <table class="dt left">
    <tr><th style="width:24%">KPI</th><th style="width:14%">Value vs screen</th><th>Read</th></tr>
    {%- for f in report.kpis.flagged[:5] %}
    <tr><td>{{ f.name }}</td><td>{{ f.value }} vs {{ f.threshold_label }}</td><td>{{ f.note }}{% if f.cite %}<sup class="cite">{{ f.cite }}</sup>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if report.kpis.other_metrics %}
  <h4 class="mini">Other operating metrics — no percentage screen applies</h4>
  <table class="dt">
    <tr><th style="width:40%">Metric</th><th>Value</th></tr>
    {%- for k in report.kpis.other_metrics %}
    <tr><td>{{ k.name }}</td><td>{{ k.value | default('—', true) }}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if report.kpis.not_extracted %}
  <h4 class="mini">Screens we could not run</h4>
  <ul class="b">
    {%- for k in report.kpis.not_extracted[:5] %}<li>{{ k.name }} — {{ k.reason }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if report.kpis.take %}<div class="take"><strong>Analyst take.</strong> {{ report.kpis.take }}</div>{% endif %}
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 7 · EARNINGS QUALITY & LEGAL
    Question: "Is the EBITDA real, and is there anything in the contracts
    that changes the price or the close?"
    Two dense sections on one page — deliberately. Neither carries a
    standalone page in a report a VP is meant to read end to end.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Earnings Quality & Legal', 7) }}
  <h2 class="section">5 · Quality of earnings</h2>

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Reported to adjusted EBITDA</h4>
      {{ chart_hbars(report.quality.addback_bars) }}
      <p class="meta">{{ report.quality.addback_caption | default('', true) }}</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Earnings quality flags</h4>
      {%- if report.quality.flags %}
      <table class="dt left">
        {%- for f in report.quality.flags[:5] %}
        <tr><td style="width:16%">{{ sev(f.severity_label, f.severity_class) }}</td><td>{{ f.text }}{% if f.cite %}<sup class="cite">{{ f.cite }}</sup>{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
      {%- else %}{{ nodata('QoE flags') }}{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section" style="margin-top:2mm;">6 · Contract and legal risk</h2>
  <div class="cols-3">
    {%- for t in report.legal.tiles[:3] %}
    <div class="tile {{ 'flag' if t.flag else '' }}"><span class="value">{{ t.value }}</span><span class="label">{{ t.label }}</span></div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- if report.legal.flags %}
  <table class="dt left">
    <tr><th style="width:16%">Severity</th><th style="width:26%">Issue</th><th>Economic or closing impact</th></tr>
    {%- for f in report.legal.flags[:5] %}
    <tr><td>{{ sev(f.severity_label, f.severity_class) }}</td><td>{{ f.issue }}</td><td>{{ f.impact }}{% if f.cite %}<sup class="cite">{{ f.cite }}</sup>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- else %}{{ nodata('Legal flags') }}{% endif %}

  {%- if report.quality.take %}<div class="take"><strong>Analyst take.</strong> {{ report.quality.take }}</div>{% endif %}
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 8 · FORECAST & VALUE CREATION
    Question: "Is the plan achievable, and what would we actually do with it?"
    Visual: forecast vs historical run-rate on the same axis as page 4, so
    the reader can see the step-up the plan assumes.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Forecast & Value Creation', 8) }}
  <h2 class="section">7 · Forecast credibility and value creation</h2>

  <h3 class="block">Plan vs Historical Run-Rate</h3>
  {{ chart_columns(report.forecast.chart) }}

  <div class="cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Assumptions that carry the plan</h4>
      {%- if report.forecast.assumptions %}
      <table class="dt left">
        <tr><th style="width:44%">Assumption</th><th style="width:20%">Support</th><th>Test</th></tr>
        {%- for a in report.forecast.assumptions[:5] %}
        <tr><td>{{ a.assumption }}</td><td>{{ sev(a.support_label, a.support_class) }}</td><td>{{ a.test }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
      {%- else %}{{ nodata('Forecast assumptions') }}{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="mini">Value creation levers</h4>
      {%- if report.forecast.levers %}
      <table class="dt left">
        <tr><th style="width:40%">Lever</th><th style="width:22%">Size</th><th>Owner of proof</th></tr>
        {%- for l in report.forecast.levers[:4] %}
        <tr><td>{{ l.lever }}</td><td>{{ l.size | default('—', true) }}</td><td>{{ l.owner | default('—', true) }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
      {%- else %}{{ nodata('Value creation levers') }}{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if report.forecast.take %}<div class="take"><strong>Analyst take.</strong> {{ report.forecast.take }}</div>{% endif %}
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 9 · RISKS, MITIGANTS & WHAT TO TEST FIRST
    Question: "What breaks the thesis, and what do we ask on Monday?"
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Risks & Next Tests', 9) }}
  <h2 class="section">8 · Risks, mitigants and what to test first</h2>

  <div class="tiles">
    {%- for h in report.risks.counts %}
    <div class="tile {{ 'flag' if h.flag else '' }}"><span class="value">{{ h.count }}</span><span class="label">{{ h.label }}</span></div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  {%- if report.risks.grid %}
  <table class="dt left">
    <tr><th style="width:13%">Severity</th><th style="width:24%">Risk</th><th style="width:31%">Evidence</th><th>Mitigant or test</th></tr>
    {%- for r in report.risks.grid[:8] %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ sev(r.severity_label, r.severity_class) }}</td>
      <td><strong>{{ r.risk }}</strong></td>
      <td>{{ r.evidence }}{% if r.cite %}<sup class="cite">{{ r.cite }}</sup>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ r.mitigant }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- if report.risks.suppressed %}
  <p class="meta">Showing the {{ report.risks.grid | length }} highest-severity risks; {{ report.risks.suppressed }} further items are in the diligence tracker.</p>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- else %}{{ nodata('Risk register') }}{% endif %}

  <h3 class="block warn">Top Questions For Management</h3>
  {%- if report.questions %}
  <ol class="q">
    {%- for q in report.questions[:8] %}
    <li><span class="cat">{{ q.category }}</span> {{ q.question }}
      {%- if q.why %}<span class="why">Why it matters: {{ q.why }}</span>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
  {%- else %}{{ nodata('Diligence questions') }}{% endif %}

  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 10 · MINIMUM PURSUIT SCORE

    THIS PAGE IS NOT A NEW DESIGN. It is the SAME MPS page the executive
    review renders — same projection (`rainmaker_view._mps_table`), same
    seven rubric rows, same score columns, same commentary bullets, same
    total row, same legend, same footer note. The only difference between
    the two documents is WHAT WAS SCORED: the executive review's run scores
    the CIM alone; this run scores the CIM plus everything else the agents
    ingested from the data room.

    Because of that, the shared markup lives in one place: `_mps_page.html.j2`,
    `{% include %}`d from both this template and
    `rainmaker_opportunity_summary.html.j2` (D-01 Path A, approved
    2026-09-07 — plan §5, T06). Do not restyle it, do not add score
    visualisations, do not re-order columns. If the two ever need to
    diverge, that is a decision to raise, not a change to make here.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page mps-page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Minimum Pursuit Score', 10) }}
  <div class="eyebrow">Minimum Pursuit Score</div>
  <h2 class="section">Does this clear Rallyday's bar for further pursuit?</h2>
  <div class="divider"></div>

  {% include "_mps_page.html.j2" %}

  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>


{#- =====================================================================
    PAGE 11 · APPENDIX — gaps, sources, run manifest
    Everything a reader needs to trust or challenge the report, and nothing
    that competes for attention with the nine pages above.
    ===================================================================== -#}
<div class="page">
  {{ running_header(report, 'Appendix', 11) }}
  <h2 class="section">Appendix</h2>

  <h3 class="block">Data Room Gaps — Information Request</h3>
  {%- if report.appendix.gaps %}
  <table class="dt left">
    <tr><th style="width:12%">Priority</th><th style="width:44%">Item requested</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>
    {%- for g in report.appendix.gaps[:10] %}
    <tr><td>{{ sev(g.priority_label, g.priority_class) }}</td><td>{{ g.item }}</td><td>{{ g.why | default('—', true) }}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- else %}<p class="nodata">No outstanding data room gaps recorded.</p>{% endif %}

  <h3 class="block">Confidence By Area</h3>
  <table class="dt left">
    <tr>{% for c in report.appendix.confidence %}<th>{{ c.area }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
    <tr>{% for c in report.appendix.confidence %}<td>{{ sev(c.level, c.level_class) }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
  </table>

  <h3 class="block">Sources Cited</h3>
  {%- if report.appendix.sources %}
  <table class="dt left">
    <tr><th style="width:8%">Ref</th><th style="width:46%">Document</th><th>Location</th></tr>
    {%- for s in report.appendix.sources %}
    <tr><td>{{ s.ref }}</td><td>{{ s.document }}</td><td>{{ s.location | default('—', true) }}</td></tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </table>
  {%- else %}<p class="nodata">Citation index not populated for this run.</p>{% endif %}

  <h3 class="block plain">Run Manifest</h3>
  <p class="meta">
    Generation mode: {{ report.meta.mode_label }} ·
    Documents indexed: {{ report.meta.doc_count | default('—', true) }} ·
    Workstreams completed: {{ report.appendix.manifest.workstreams_ok | default('—', true) }} of {{ report.appendix.manifest.workstreams_total | default('—', true) }} ·
    Degraded workstreams: {{ report.appendix.manifest.degraded | default('none', true) }} ·
    Template version {{ report.meta.template_version | default('final_report.html.j2 v0.1', true) }}
  </p>
  <p class="meta">{{ report.meta.status }}</p>
  {{ page_footer(report) }}
</div>

</body>
</html>
